"""Generated file — do not edit by hand.

Display metadata (channel title, avatar URL) for every channel the onboarding
wizard suggests, keyed by YouTube channel id. Written by
scripts/resolve_genre_artists.py; regenerate with

    .venv/bin/python -m scripts.resolve_genre_artists

Why this is committed rather than resolved per install: spotea is self-hosted,
so every operator running the resolution themselves would mean every operator
paying ~600 yt-dlp calls from their own IP — and, until they did, a wizard that
sat on "Finding channels…" for minutes on the first pick of each genre. Paying
it once here means a fresh clone serves a full wizard having never contacted
YouTube. See app/services/genre_artists.py's module docstring.

Avatar URLs are safe to freeze into a file: they are content-addressed (a hash
path plus a size suffix, no signature and no expiry — checked against a live
extraction). They do go stale when a channel changes its picture, at which
point the URL stops resolving and that card falls back to the same grey circle
a channel with no avatar gets (see app/main.py's avatar_proxy). Re-running the
generator picks up the new URLs.

Deliberately no subscriber counts: the wizard has never displayed one, and a
number frozen at generation time is the one field here that would rot into
being wrong rather than merely absent.

The curated channel lists themselves are hand-maintained elsewhere and are not
touched by the generator — see scripts/seed_music_artists.py and
scripts/seed_podcast_channels.py.
"""




